"""Player-facing text for quirks and powers.

Two tables, both keyed by quirk id:

  QUIRK_HINT  shown in the tracking menu while a quirk is still LOCKED.
              In-character, tied to the figure the quirk is named for.
              It points at the kind of thing to do without naming the
              number or the exact condition -- the discovery is the fun.

  QUIRK_DESC  shown once a quirk is UNLOCKED (tracking menu and the
              unlock popup). Says in plain words what the reward does,
              then a line of flavor.

The short reward line (`_QUIRK_EFFECTS`), the exact trigger
(`_QUIRK_TRIGGER`) and the unlock quote (`_QUIRK_FLAVOR`) stay in
quirk_system.py. tests/test_quirk_text.py asserts every quirk has an
entry in both tables and that no hint quotes its own threshold.
"""

# What each stat does, appended to rewards that raise it.
